# markets2day — project rules for Cursor

## Stack
- Expo (React Native), managed workflow — no custom native code unless explicitly necessary
- Styling: NativeWind (Tailwind classes for RN)
- Backend: Supabase (Postgres + PostGIS, Auth, Storage) via `src/lib/supabase.js`
- Navigation: React Navigation (bottom tabs + native stack for the market detail screen)
- Fonts: Bebas Neue (display/headers), Work Sans (body) — loaded via expo-font

## Design system
Always use the color tokens and font names from `src/constants/theme.ts`. Never invent new
hex colors — if a new shade is genuinely needed, add it to theme.ts first and explain why.

Palette:
- paper #F3ECDD (background)
- card #FBF8F2 (surfaces)
- ink #2E2015 (primary text)
- inkSoft #8A7862 (secondary text)
- burgundy #7A2A34 / burgundyDark #4A1017 (primary accent, CTAs, organiser-verified)
- blue #9DBBDA / blueDark #3E5F82 (secondary accent, community-verified, links)
- sand #C9AE82 / sandDark #8F7350 (tertiary accent)
- brown #4A3423 (neutral accent)
- line #E4D9C3 (borders/dividers)

## Data model
Match the Supabase schema exactly (see project docs) — table names: profiles, markets,
market_photos, confirmations, reviews, saved_markets. Never guess a column name; ask if unsure.

## Conventions
- Before creating a new component, check `src/components/` for an existing one that fits.
- One feature/screen per change — keep diffs small and reviewable.
- Use functional components and hooks only.
- Prefer Expo SDK packages (expo-location, expo-notifications, expo-image-picker,
  expo-sharing) over third-party alternatives when Expo has an equivalent.
- Never hardcode Supabase URL/keys — always read from `process.env.EXPO_PUBLIC_*`.
